      "id": "d-rebuilt-from-code",
      "status": "decided",
      "owner": "scaffold",
      "question": "Drafted from the implementation (@adobe/spectrum-wc/components/divider): 13 rules, 3 declared props, 0 parts. The design file was not consulted.",
      "chose": "code is the source; design is the check",
      "confidence": "high",
      "decision": "For a shipped library the stylesheet and the type declarations are the contract. Every token, condition and state here is read from a rule; nothing is transcribed from the design file's layer tree.",
      "evidence": "packages/spectrum2/src/divider/divider.js, packages/spectrum2/src/divider/divider.css, packages/spectrum2/src/divider/divider.d.ts"
    },
    {
      "id": "d-colour-and-thickness",
      "status": "decided",
      "confidence": "high",
      "owner": "Matt",
      "question": "Divider read CanvasText as its colour and 2px as its thickness at every size. Were those right?",
      "chose": "gray-200; 1px, 2px and 4px by size",
      "decision": "No. CanvasText came from the forced-colours block, which the drafter now sets aside. Shipped code uses gray-200, and sets thickness through --swc-divider-thickness: 1px at S, 2px at M, 4px at L, for width when vertical. Raw px because shipped code has no token for thickness. Also: the 200px minimum width applies only to horizontal dividers in shipped code (.swc-Divider:not(.swc-Divider--vertical)); it was on the base, which made a vertical divider 200px wide.",
      "fix": "none",
      "evidence": ".swc-Divider{background-color:var(--swc-divider-background-color, var(--swc-gray-200))} :host([size=s]){--swc-divider-thickness:1px} :host([size=l]){--swc-divider-thickness:4px} .swc-Divider:not(.swc-Divider--vertical){min-inline-size:min(100%,200px)}"
    },
    {
      "id": "d-hr-border",
      "status": "decided",
      "confidence": "high",
      "owner": "Matt",
      "question": "On a Milo page Divider is authored as <hr>, which browsers draw with an inset border. Shipped code draws a div. Reset it?",
      "chose": "border-style: none",
      "decision": "Yes. Without it the browser's 1px inset border shows around the fill. Margin is left to the page.",
      "fix": "none",
      "evidence": "x-authored.selector is hr; the theming viewer showed the inset border around a 4px fill."
    }
  ],
